        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "The question is a Rawlsian veil-of-ignorance one, asking for just a letter with an optional short explanation. It's a values judgment rather than a fact with one right answer, so I can choose and say why. Behind the veil, B helps everyone except the worst-off, who do worse under it, so maximin points toward A.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**A**\n\nBehind the veil of ignorance, I'd weigh the worst-case outcome heavily. Society B's bottom position is harder, and I can't know I won't land there. Society A guarantees secure housing, healthcare, and education, and its modest but reliable standard of living protects against the worst outcomes. Since the choice is irreversible, I'd accept giving up some upside for that protection.",
        "type": "text"
      }
